              item        : "ip ssh version 2[\\s]*$"
            </item>

            <item>
              type        : CONFIG_CHECK
              description : "http secure-server"
              item        : "ip http secure-server"
            </item>

            <item>
              type        : CONFIG_CHECK
              description : "http secure-ciphersuite"
              item        : "ip http secure-ciphersuite aes-(128|256)-cbc-sha"
            </item>

            <item>
              type        : CONFIG_CHECK
              description : "ssh server algorithm"
              item        : "ip ssh server algorithm encryption (?=.*aes256-ctr ?)(?=.*aes192-ctr ?)(?=.*aes128-ctr ?)"
            </item>

            <item>
              type        : CONFIG_CHECK
              description : "http secure-trustpoint"
              item        : "ip http secure-trustpoint [^ ]+"
            </item>

            <item>
              type        : CONFIG_CHECK
              description : "http secure-client-auth"
              item        : "ip http secure-client-auth"
            </item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.34 CISC-ND-001210"
              info        : "The Cisco router must be configured to implement cryptographic mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of remote maintenance sessions.

GROUP ID: V-215700
RULE ID: SV-215700r879785

This requires the use of secure protocols instead of their unsecured counterparts, such as SSH instead of telnet, SCP instead of FTP, and HTTPS instead of HTTP. If unsecured protocols (lacking cryptographic mechanisms) are used for sessions, the contents of those sessions will be susceptible to eavesdropping, potentially putting sensitive data (including administrator passwords) at risk of compromise and potentially allowing hijacking of maintenance sessions."
              solution    : "Configure the Cisco router to implement cryptographic mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of remote maintenance sessions using a FIPS 140-2 approved algorithm as shown in the examples below.

SSH Example

R1(config)#ip ssh server algorithm encryption aes256-ctr aes192-ctr aes128-ctr

HTTPS Example

R2(config)#ip http secure-ciphersuite aes-128-cbc-sha"
              reference   : "800-171|3.7.5,800-171r3|03.07.05,800-53|MA-4(6),800-53r5|MA-4(6),CAT|I,CCI|CCI-003123,CSF|PR.MA-2,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|MA-4(6),LEVEL|1A,NESA|T2.3.4,NESA|T5.4.4,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,Rule-ID|SV-215700r879785_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-ND-001210,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.6,TBA-FIISB|45.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-215700"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26598"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </then>

